INT. FAMILY LAW OFFICE, WAITING ROOM - DAY

Plastic chairs. A dying ficus. A wall clock that runs four minutes slow.

FIONA KESSELL, 40s, in a suit, clutches a folder. GIDEON KESSELL, 40s, her ex, ankle on his knee, scrolls his phone. HANA OKADA, 30s, Fiona's sister, perches beside her. IVO BRAJOVIC, 60s, Gideon's father, sits stiff with his coat on. JOLENE MARCH, 30s, Gideon's new girlfriend, carries two coffees. And KASPAR, 10, Fiona and Gideon's son, swings his legs on a chair too tall.

Jolene offers a coffee to Fiona. Fiona doesn't take it. Hana takes it instead. Jolene smiles and sits.

HANA
Thanks.

JOLENE
You're welcome.

Fiona stares at the ficus. Gideon taps his screen. Ivo clears his throat.

IVO
Gideon.

GIDEON
Dad.

IVO
Put the phone away.

GIDEON
It's work.

FIONA
It's never work.

GIDEON
(not looking up)
Fiona, not here.

FIONA
Where, then?

GIDEON
In there. With the lawyer.

KASPAR
Mom, can I have a coffee?

FIONA
No.

JOLENE
(to Kaspar)
I'll get you a hot chocolate, sweetheart.

FIONA
Don't call him that.

JOLENE
I'm sorry?

FIONA
Sweetheart.

Hana stands. Fiona stands. Jolene stands. Gideon rises last. Ivo folds his arms. Kaspar slides off the chair, backs into the corner, and the five adults square off, voices rising, hands moving, until the door opens and a receptionist leans out.

Everyone freezes.

HANA
(quietly)
Sorry.

She sits. They all sit. Kaspar slips back into his chair. Fiona accepts the coffee, finally.
